#: ../../../gallery/embellishments/pygmtlogo.rst:22
msgid "PyGMT logo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/embellishments/pygmtlogo.rst:23
msgid ""
"Beside the :doc:`GMT logo </gallery/embellishments/gmt_logo>`, there is a "
"specific logo for PyGMT which can be plotted and added to a figure using :"
"meth:`pygmt.Figure.pygmtlogo`. The design of the logo itself is kindly "
"provided by `@sfrooti <https://github.com/sfrooti>`_ and consists of an icon "
"and the wordmark \"PyGMT\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/embellishments/pygmtlogo.rst:29
msgid ""
"The visual logo is available in circle and hexagon shapes. It supports both "
"colored and monochrome black-and-white palettes, alongside light and dark "
"theme modes, combining to yield eight distinct standalone logo variants. "
"Additionally, the visual logo can optionally include the wordmark \"PyGMT\"; "
"if enabled, the wordmark can be positioned either to the right of the icon "
"or beneath it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/embellishments/pygmtlogo.rst:37
msgid ""
"import pygmt\n"
"from pygmt.params import Frame"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/embellishments/pygmtlogo.rst:45
msgid "Plot the PyGMT logo without any arguments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/embellishments/pygmtlogo.rst:49
msgid ""
"fig = pygmt.Figure()\n"
"fig.pygmtlogo()\n"
"fig.show()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/embellishments/pygmtlogo.rst:60
msgid ""
"Via the ``color``, ``theme``, ``shape`` parameters the appearance of the "
"logo can be changed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/embellishments/pygmtlogo.rst:65
msgid ""
"fig = pygmt.Figure()\n"
"fig.basemap(region=[-1, 1] * 2, projection=\"X5c/5c\", "
"frame=Frame(fill=\"180/199/231\"))\n"
"\n"
"fig.pygmtlogo(color=False, position=\"TL\")\n"
"\n"
"fig.pygmtlogo(theme=\"dark\", position=\"TR\")\n"
"\n"
"fig.pygmtlogo(color=False, theme=\"dark\", position=\"BL\")\n"
"\n"
"fig.pygmtlogo(shape=\"hexagon\", position=\"BR\")\n"
"\n"
"fig.show()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/embellishments/pygmtlogo.rst:85
msgid ""
"Via the ``wordamrk`` parameter the text \"PyGMT\" can be added on the right "
"side or at the bottom of the visual. Use the ``width`` and ``height`` "
"parameters to adjust the size of the logo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/embellishments/pygmtlogo.rst:91
msgid ""
"fig = pygmt.Figure()\n"
"fig.basemap(region=[-1, 1] * 2, projection=\"X7c/5c\", "
"frame=Frame(fill=\"180/199/231\"))\n"
"\n"
"fig.pygmtlogo(wordmark=\"horizontal\", position=\"TC\", width=\"6c\")\n"
"\n"
"fig.pygmtlogo(theme=\"dark\", wordmark=\"vertical\", position=\"BC\", "
"height=\"3c\")\n"
"\n"
"fig.show()"
msgstr ""

